      "source_text": "Work noise-free ($R = 0$, $\\lambda \\to 0$, so $\\mu_t = s$ is the minimum-norm interpolant of the data and $\\sigma_t^2$ is the power function). (a) Assume $K_t$ is invertible (for example, distinct inputs with a strictly positive-definite kernel), $B_{\\mathrm{true}} \\ge \\|s\\|_k$ and $\\sigma_t(x) \\gt 0$. Show that there is an $f \\in \\mathcal{H}_k$ interpolating the data with $\\|f\\|_k = B_{\\mathrm{true}}$ and $f(x) = s(x) - \\sqrt{B_{\\mathrm{true}}^2 - \\|s\\|_k^2}\\;\\sigma_t(x)$. (b) Conclude that the Real-$\\beta$ lower bound with $B_{\\mathrm{est}} \\lt \\sqrt{B_{\\mathrm{true}}^2 - \\|s\\|_k^2}$ is violated at $x$, and construct a three-point domain on which this produces an unsafe query.",
